  "description": "Sealed envelope vectors. All keys are test-only values: recipient keys are the push.pair fixture host key (bytes 0x20..0x3f) and device key (bytes 0x40..0x5f); ephPriv and nonce are SHA-256(\"togo test vector: \" + name + \" ephemeral\") and the first 12 bytes of SHA-256(\"togo test vector: \" + name + \" nonce\"). Encoding: keys, nonce, sharedSecret, salt, key and ciphertext are lowercase hex; label, info, aad and plaintext are UTF-8 strings; envelope is base64url without padding. Steps: sharedSecret = X25519(ephPriv, recipientPub), rejected when all zero; salt = ephPub || recipientPub; key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm=sharedSecret, salt, info=\"togo/v1/\" + label, L=32); ciphertext = ChaCha20-Poly1305(key, nonce, plaintext, aad), ciphertext then 16-byte tag; envelope = 0x01 || ephPub || nonce || ciphertext. vectors: sealing with ephPriv and nonce must reproduce envelope byte for byte, and opening with recipientPriv must return plaintext. negative: opening envelope with recipientPriv, label and aad must fail without revealing which check failed (bad base64url, version not 0x01, shorter than 61 bytes, low-order ephemeral key, wrong label, aad or key, tampered bytes).",
